{
  "id": "30154_seku",
  "headword": "{急|せ}く",
  "reading": "せく",
  "romaji": "seku",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-godan",
  "gloss": "to be in a rush; to feel impatient",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be hurried; to feel rushed; to be impatient",
      "explanation": "For a person's mind or breathing to be driven forward by impatience. Intransitive, and most often used of {気|き} (one's feelings) or {息|いき} (one's breath)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30154_seku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{気|き}が{急|せ}いて{落|お}ち{着|つ}かない。",
      "english": "I feel rushed and can't settle down.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30154_seku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{階段|かいだん}を{上|のぼ}ったら{息|いき}が{急|せ}いた。",
      "english": "My breath came short after I climbed the stairs.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30154_seku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{締|し}め{切|き}りが{近|ちか}づくにつれて{気|き}が{急|せ}き、{細|こま}かい{確認|かくにん}を{忘|わす}れてしまった。",
      "english": "As the deadline drew near I grew impatient and forgot to check the details.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "An older, somewhat literary verb that survives mainly in set phrases. It describes the internal feeling of being hurried, not the act of hurrying.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {気|き}が{急|せ}く: to feel rushed, to be impatient\n- {息|いき}が{急|せ}く: for one's breathing to become short\n- {急|せ}いては{事|こと}を{仕損|しそん}じる: haste makes waste (proverb)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {急|いそ}ぐ: to hurry — the ordinary word, describing the action of moving fast\n- {焦|あせ}る: to be flustered — stronger, with a sense of anxiety about falling behind\n\nRELATED FORMS:\nせっかち (impatient, hasty) derives from this verb.",
